## MULTI-PRODUCT IMAGE HANDLING

**CRITICAL:** This section applies multi-item concepts to catalog products.

When an image contains multiple products, you MUST output an actionable manifest that downstream agents can execute.

### Domain Vocabulary Mapping

| Generic Term | Catalog Meaning |
|--------------|-----------------|
| Item | Product |
| VARIANTS | Same product type, different size/color/design (complete products in grid) |
| COLLECTION | Different product types (e.g., jar + lid + label in same image) |
| COMPONENTS | **Different PARTS across multiple images** (bodies in one, lids in another) -> COMPOSE together |
| Variant Axes | Size, Color, Design, Material |

**CRITICAL DISTINCTION:**
- **VARIANTS** = Complete products in a grid -> EXTRACT each individually
- **COMPONENTS** = Incomplete parts across images -> COMPOSE into complete products

### Classification Matrix

| Observation | Classification | Catalog Implication |
|-------------|----------------|---------------------|
| Same product, multiple angles | SINGLE_ITEM | One SKU, multiple assets |
| Same product type, different sizes | VARIANTS | Multiple SKUs, same family |
| Same product type, different colors/designs | VARIANTS | Multiple SKUs, variant axis |
| Different product types | COLLECTION | Multiple families or bundled set |
| Product with accessories | COLLECTION | Main product + accessory SKUs |
| **Different images contain different PARTS** (bodies, lids, accessories) | **COMPONENTS** | **COMPOSE parts into complete product shots** |

### Multi-Product Output Template (MANDATORY FORMAT)

When multi-product detected, output this EXACT structure:

```markdown
## MULTI-ITEM ASSESSMENT

- **Count:** [N products]
- **Classification:** [VARIANTS | COLLECTION | COMPONENTS]
- **Rationale:** [Why this classification - what visual evidence]

### Variant Axes (if VARIANTS)

| Axis | Values Found |
|------|--------------|
| Size | [e.g., Large, Medium, Small] |
| Color | [e.g., Blue, Yellow, Pink] |
| Design | [e.g., Blossoms, Charming Flowers, Spring Flowers] |

### Extraction Targets (with Bounding Boxes)

| # | Description | BBox [y_min, x_min, y_max, x_max] | Position | Size | Color | Design |
|---|-------------|-----------------------------------|----------|------|-------|--------|
| 1 | [Full description] | [estimated bounds for item 1] | [position] | [Size] | [Color] | [Design] |
| 2 | [Full description] | [estimated bounds for item 2] | [position] | [Size] | [Color] | [Design] |
| ... | ... | ... | ... | ... | ... | ... |

**CRITICAL:** BBox coordinates are MANDATORY for downstream extraction.
- Coordinates: [y_min, x_min, y_max, x_max] normalized to 0-1000 scale
- Origin: top-left corner of image
- Estimate bounds by mentally dividing image into 1000x1000 grid
- Each item gets UNIQUE coordinates based on its ACTUAL position in the image

### Processing Strategies

| Strategy | Result | Recommended When |
|----------|--------|------------------|
| INDIVIDUAL | [N] hero shots, one per SKU | Catalog work, product pages |
| BY_SIZE | [M] shots grouped by size | Size comparison graphics |
| BY_DESIGN | [M] shots grouped by design | Design showcase |
| COMPOSITE | 1 family shot | Marketing, range display |

**Default for catalog:** INDIVIDUAL (each product needs its own hero shot)
**For marketing request:** COMPOSITE (family/range shot)
```

### Position Vocabulary

See `multi_item.protocol` (domain=creative) for the full position vocabulary (top-left, center, foreground, row-1, etc.).

### Canonical Example: 9-Jar Variant Set

```markdown
## MULTI-ITEM ASSESSMENT

- **Count:** 9 products
- **Classification:** VARIANTS
- **Rationale:** Same jar type in 3 sizes x 3 designs, identical form factor

### Variant Axes

| Axis | Values Found |
|------|--------------|
| Size | [Size A] ([volume A]), [Size B] ([volume B]), [Size C] ([volume C]) |
| Design | [Design A] ([color A] lid), [Design B] ([color B] lid), [Design C] ([color C] lid) |

### Extraction Targets (with Bounding Boxes)

| # | Description | BBox [y_min, x_min, y_max, x_max] | Position | Size | Design |
|---|-------------|-----------------------------------|----------|------|--------|
| 1 | [Size A] [product] with [color A] lid, [Design A] print | [row1_y_start, col1_x_start, row1_y_end, col1_x_end] | top-left | [Size A] | [Design A] |
| 2 | [Size A] [product] with [color B] lid, [Design B] print | [row1_y_start, col2_x_start, row1_y_end, col2_x_end] | top-center | [Size A] | [Design B] |
| 3 | [Size A] [product] with [color C] lid, [Design C] print | [row1_y_start, col3_x_start, row1_y_end, col3_x_end] | top-right | [Size A] | [Design C] |
| 4 | [Size B] [product] with [color A] lid, [Design A] print | [row2_y_start, col1_x_start, row2_y_end, col1_x_end] | middle-left | [Size B] | [Design A] |
| 5 | [Size B] [product] with [color B] lid, [Design B] print | [row2_y_start, col2_x_start, row2_y_end, col2_x_end] | middle-center | [Size B] | [Design B] |
| 6 | [Size B] [product] with [color C] lid, [Design C] print | [row2_y_start, col3_x_start, row2_y_end, col3_x_end] | middle-right | [Size B] | [Design C] |
| 7 | [Size C] [product] with [color A] lid, [Design A] print | [row3_y_start, col1_x_start, row3_y_end, col1_x_end] | bottom-left | [Size C] | [Design A] |
| 8 | [Size C] [product] with [color B] lid, [Design B] print | [row3_y_start, col2_x_start, row3_y_end, col2_x_end] | bottom-center | [Size C] | [Design B] |
| 9 | [Size C] [product] with [color C] lid, [Design C] print | [row3_y_start, col3_x_start, row3_y_end, col3_x_end] | bottom-right | [Size C] | [Design C] |

**Coordinate Estimation:** For 3x3 grid, divide 1000 by 3 for boundaries. Row 1 starts at 0, Row 2 at ~333, Row 3 at ~666. Same for columns.

### Processing Strategies

| Strategy | Result | Recommended When |
|----------|--------|------------------|
| INDIVIDUAL | N hero shots | Catalog (each SKU needs asset) |
| BY_SIZE | M shots (one per size) | Size comparison |
| BY_DESIGN | K shots (one per design) | Design showcase |
| COMPOSITE | 1 family shot | Marketing, range display |

**Default for catalog:** INDIVIDUAL
```

### Key Signals

| Signal | Classification | Variant Axes |
|--------|----------------|--------------|
| Identical shape, different scales | VARIANTS | Size |
| Same shape, different colors | VARIANTS | Color |
| Same shape, different patterns/prints | VARIANTS | Design |
| Different shapes entirely | COLLECTION | N/A |
| Product + cap/lid separately | COLLECTION | N/A |
| Same product from multiple angles | SINGLE_ITEM | N/A |

### COMPONENTS Detection (CRITICAL - Cross-Image Analysis)

**When analyzing MULTIPLE images, check if they show different PARTS of products:**

| Cross-Image Signal | Classification | Action |
|--------------------|----------------|--------|
| Image A has bodies, Image B has lids | **COMPONENTS** | Parts to COMPOSE into complete products |
| Image A has products, Image B has accessories (spoons, handles) | **COMPONENTS** | Accessories to ADD to products |
| Each image has same product type but dismantled | **COMPONENTS** | Reassemble for hero shots |
| Grid of bodies + separate image with lids array | **COMPONENTS** | Match and compose |

**COMPONENTS Output Template:**

```markdown
## MULTI-IMAGE ASSESSMENT

- **Classification:** COMPONENTS
- **Rationale:** Multiple images contain different PARTS of complete products

### Component Images

| Image | Contains | Count | Notes |
|-------|----------|-------|-------|
| [path1] | Jar bodies | 9 (3x3 grid) | Main product bodies |
| [path2] | Colored lids | 4 colors | Lid accessories |
| [path3] | Measuring spoons | 4 colors | Spoon accessories |

### Composition Matrix

| Variant | Body From | Lid From | Accessory From |
|---------|-----------|----------|----------------|
| Large Blue | [path1] top-left | [path2] blue lid | [path3] blue spoon |
| Large Yellow | [path1] mid-left | [path2] yellow lid | [path3] yellow spoon |
| ... | ... | ... | ... |

### CRITICAL - Processing Strategy

**COMPOSE, don't just EXTRACT.**

Each hero shot should combine:
1. Body from grid image (extraction)
2. Matching lid from lid image (overlay/composite)
3. Accessory from accessory image (positioned beside)

Use image_studio with multiple labeled images:
```
images=[
  {path: 'grid.jpg', label: 'body'},
  {path: 'lids.jpg', label: 'lid'},
  {path: 'spoons.jpg', label: 'accessory'}
]
composition={position: '[body] center, [lid] on top, [accessory] beside'}
```
```

**Anti-Pattern:** Treating COMPONENTS as VARIANTS and just extracting from grid - results in incomplete products (bodies without lids).

---

## OUTPUT FILE (CRITICAL)

Write analysis to file with unique name derived from source image.

**Pattern:**
```
/main/visual_analysis_{image_basename}.md
```

**Example:**
- Source image: `inbox/user123/20251217_152547_photo.jpg`
- Output file: `/main/visual_analysis_20251217_152547_photo.md`

**Why unique names matter:**
- Generic names like `catalog_analysis.md` get OVERWRITTEN on next analysis
- Unique names enable PM to reference correct analysis in downstream delegations
- Downstream agents (catalog_analyst, catalog_specialist) need stable file paths

---

## INTEGRATION WITH OTHER PROTOCOLS

After visual analysis, proceed to:

1. **research_product** - Verify material specs, pricing
2. **family_fit** - Use target customer insight for family matching
3. **duplicate_prevention** - Use visual details for comparison
4. **pricing** - Use market positioning for price range

---

## ANTI-PATTERNS

| Anti-Pattern | Problem | Correct Approach |
|--------------|---------|------------------|
| Surface-level analysis | "This is a plastic bottle" | Full detail: "[size] [material] [product], [texture], [closure], [finish], [segment] positioning" |
| Material-only focus | Only identify material | Material + Form + Features + Target Customer - all four inform decisions |
| Ignoring target customer | "[material] [product] = [material] family" | Consider finish and positioning: "Premium finish suggests D2C cosmetic, check cosmetic families" |

</protocol>
